SWEET Bluetooth: full-sequence replay probe + 0x200b status rewrite knob + full tx dump (patch 0217, ticket T-4c2c, W-BTUP; boot-arg sweetbtleprobe=2 gates the replay, sweetbtrw200b=1 the rewrite, default behaviour unchanged, sweetbtleprobe=1 unchanged). bt-up5 [obs 20261104T054627Z-bt-up5]: the 0216 matrix got 0x2007/0x200b status 0 after every LE command bluetoothd sends, yet bluetoothd's own run got 0x2007 status 0x0c at its command position 49 (right after vendor 0xfd48, decode of merged.log lines 1762-2046) and 0x200b status 0x0c at position ~67, then exits. The flip therefore sits in positions 21-48 (classic setup 0c33..0c52, 0c24/0c47/0c1c, vendor fd3c fce9 fce2 fd48). The replay (sweetbtleprobe=2) sends bluetoothd's commands 1..48 in order (byte for byte from the trace except the two payloads the trace cut at 24 bytes, 0c13 name and 0c52 EIR: visible prefix + zeros, announced by a `payload truncated` row) after the baud-probe Reset and sends the read-only 0x2007 after every step; the first status != 0 logs `BT PROBE: first-disallowed-after=<pos> op=<op>`, with two witnesses at the flip (bluetoothd's 0x200b, LE Set Scan Enable OFF once; never an enable). If no step flips, it asks 0x200b after the last step and again after a 25 s wait (timing hypothesis). sbu_cmd now takes payloads up to 255 bytes (was 8). Every replayed opcode was sent byte-exact to this ROM by bluetoothd itself in bt-up5 (fd3c/fce9/fce2/0c13/0c52 also in bt-up4; the fd48 payload differs per instance and the ROM answers 0x01; Opus review T-4c2c #3): volatile controller RAM state, cleared by the REG_ON power-cycle that follows the probe (same path as 0216). sweetbtrw200b=1: the rx stream to bluetoothd is parsed as H4 events and the status byte of a Command Complete for opcode 0x200b is rewritten from 0x0c to 0x00, one `BT GAP:` row per rewrite (diagnostic knob that scores bluetoothd's alive_s and names its next exit cause, not a fix; the chip still refused the command; no register store; the HCI trace shows the chip's real bytes). The HCI trace now dumps host->chip packets longer than 24 bytes in full as `BT HCI: tx data@<offset>:` rows (<= 262 bytes), so the next replay is byte-exact (this dump also runs on every sweetbt=1 boot: log rows only, a third knob vs bt-up5). The rewrite parser resets its framing after an rx error and switches itself off on an ACL/SCO/ISO packet type (review T-4c2c #4). Applies after 0189, 0213, 0215 and 0216. Not run on hardware yet.

